.TH smi-nginx-fix-permissions "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-nginx-fix-permissions \- Set owners, modes and SELinux labels of the nginx configuration and keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-nginx-fix-permissions
.RB [ \-n ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-nginx-fix-permissions
sets the configuration and the private keys of nginx, and of HAProxy when it is installed, to what
the services need and no more:
.PP
.RS
.nf
/etc/nginx                             root:root   0755 dirs  0644 files
/etc/nginx/conf.d/draft-tokens.map     root:root   0600
/etc/pki/nginx                         root:root   0755 dirs  0644 certificates
/etc/pki/nginx/private                 root:nginx  0750       0640 keys
/var/log/nginx                         nginx:root  0700
/etc/systemd/system/nginx.service.d    root:root   0755       0644
.fi
.RE
.PP
and, only when
.I /etc/haproxy
exists and the
.B haproxy
group does:
.PP
.RS
.nf
/etc/haproxy                           root:root      0755 dirs  0644 files
/etc/haproxy/vhosts/draft-tokens.lst   root:root      0600
/etc/pki/haproxy                       root:haproxy   0750       0640 combined PEM files
/etc/systemd/system/haproxy.service.d  root:root      0755       0644
.fi
.RE
.PP
The SELinux labels of those paths are restored with
.B restorecon -RF
when
.BR restorecon (8)
is installed.
A path that does not exist is skipped.
The command refuses to run when the
.B nginx
group is missing, which means nginx is not installed.
It has to be run as root.
.PP
Afterwards it checks what matters: that the
.B nginx
user can read each key in
.IR /etc/pki/nginx/private ,
that the
.B haproxy
user can read each PEM file in
.IR /etc/pki/haproxy ,
and that no file under
.I /etc/nginx
is group or world writable.
Each finding is reported and counted, and the command ends with
.B 1
when any are left.
.PP
The served content is not touched;
.BR smi-nginx-fix-content (1)
does that.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
Dry run: print the commands that would change something, prefixed with
.BR "would run" ,
and change nothing. The checks still run and are still reported.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Everything was set and nothing was found to report.
.TP
.B 1
Not root, an unknown argument, no
.B nginx
group, or findings were reported.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
After changing the configuration or installing a certificate:
.RS
.nf
sudo smi-nginx-fix-permissions -n
sudo smi-nginx-fix-permissions
sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
.PP
Report smi-nginx-fix-permissions bugs to \fIinfo@setmy.info\fR
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
